{
 "translation": "So, to implement the 'Embrace in your heart' program, this committee of neighborhood Mullah Shakur organized several morning processions. Four or five in the morning was the most opportune time for them. There was no noise from people, no traffic congestion. Even the dogs, who had been on guard duty all night, would be lying with their heads buried in extinguished ovens. People, huddled in their beds, would hear the voices of the morning procession participants and just say, \"Oh, it's that same group again!\" And then, sometimes with patience and sometimes with irritation, they would listen to Babu Sundarlal's propaganda. Those women who had safely reached the other side would lie spread out like cauliflower florets, and their husbands, stiff like stalks beside them, would protest the noise of the morning procession, muttering something under their breath as they went along. Or somewhere, a child would open their eyes for a little while, and understanding the 'Embrace in your heart' program's plaintive and sorrowful propaganda as just a song, would fall back asleep.",
